  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday Night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1113 AM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nThe weak, diffuse surface front from the Ohio Valley will dip into\nMiddle TN Thursday night before stalling out. This frontal zone,\nalong with a series of weak shortwaves, will bring increasing \nchances for showers and storms Friday and especially Saturday. \nRain chances will peak in the 60 to 80 percent range Saturday \nafternoon. In spite of low to medium rain chances Friday and \nmedium to high chances Saturday, conditions will stay hot and \nhumid with highs in the lower 90s and max heat index values around\n100. The high humidity and storm chances will bring potential for\nlocal heavy downpours, but we are not looking for widespread \nflooding or severe storms thanks to weak forcing, poor lapse \nrates, and generally weak atmospheric winds. \n\nUnfortunately, models show the buildup of another strong ridge \npattern next week. Highs may climb into the mid 90s again and we \nmay be looking at heat headlines for many areas by Tuesday.",
